      "items": [
        {
          "headline": "Members of Congress call for Jensen Huang to resign and press to put three chip-export bills in the NDAA",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "CNBC", "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/11/nvidia-jensen-huang-congress-resign-ai-chips.html" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "CNBC reports that Senate banking committee member Kevin Cramer, R-N.D., \"doubled down Wednesday on his call for Huang to resign\", telling CNBC \"as a matter of his own conscience, he should resign\" and that Huang is \"right now so vulnerable to extortion, blackmail. I just don't think, as a national security matter, we can run the risk.\" Rep. Suhas Subramanyam, D-Va., and Rep. Don Bacon, R-Neb., also said he should step down.",
            "Wednesday was the deadline set by three House chairs — Brian Mast (Foreign Affairs), John Moolenaar (Select Committee on China) and Rick Crawford (intelligence) — who asked Huang to testify on Nov. 18 in a Nov. 4 letter. CNBC says they had not heard from him; asked whether they would consider a subpoena, Mast said \"yes\", and Moolenaar said \"all three committees have subpoena power\".",
